A||N||26||TTiger||3800 SC exhaust question||||5||
Z||000000||TTiger||12-11-2001||02:48 AM||||Right now I am at a wall in my 3800 SC conversion and I am seeking some opinions.  I am trying to figure out what to do with my exhaust to get the most power from the conversion.  I also need to keep my Fiero emissions legal.  Right now I have the engine mounted on the cradle along with my original exhaust, and I can't see any way to make them work together (exhaust exits the wrong side of the engine  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> )<P>Any ideas?<P>Tony||||reg||5
Z||000001||West Coast Fiero||12-11-2001||02:56 AM||||We here at West Coast Fiero offer an exhaust system that utilizes equal length exhuast primaries. Check out our website for further details<BR> <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <P><P>------------------<BR>Technician, West Coast Fiero<BR>www.cwestco.com<BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000002||fieroX||12-11-2001||03:03 AM||||Im building headers for mine with 1 3/4" primaries, and 2 1/2 collectors into a 3" single pipe to the muffler and dual 2 1/2" outlets.  I do have one major advantage in that we dont have emmissions testing here, so Im running my crossover toward the rear of the car and my 3" pipe will snake down past the tranny and into the muffler, instead of running all the way under the front of the cradle, around the passenger side, and into the muffler at the back of the car.  If someone makes a real small cat this kind of setup could be possible, but difficult.  There isnt much room in there.  Check out my website in a few weeks, as I will be starting my exhaust venture.  Good luck!<P>------------------<BR>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroX.com" TARGET=_blank>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fierox.com/logo2small.gif">  </A><BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroX.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroX.com</A><BR>coming soon L67 powered 87 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000003||West Coast Fiero||12-11-2001||03:11 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by West Coast Fiero:<BR><B>We here at West Coast Fiero offer an exhaust system that utilizes equal length exhuast primaries. Check out our website for further details<BR> <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <P><BR>I neglected to mention that these headers are smog legal as they do have all neccassary adaptations for smog equipment, and carry the exhaust system to the existing lower Fiero exhaust<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>Technician, West Coast Fiero<BR>www.cwestco.com<BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000004||fieroX||12-11-2001||03:15 AM||||Oh yeah, and my headers will be EGR delete, as it adds heat into the combustion chamber, which increases KR, decreases power and carbon ups the blower rotors.  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||TTiger||12-11-2001||03:17 AM||||Thanks West Coast Fiero.  Your site was the first that I checked when I ran into this problem 2 months ago.  Unfortunately, I don't think I want to replace the exhaust headers quite yet.<P>fieroX, I will keep an eye on your site.  Keep me posted.  I have been trying to find a way to fabricate a system that will work with the limited room.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||West Coast Fiero||12-11-2001||04:33 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by TTiger:<BR><B>Thanks West Coast Fiero.  Your site was the first that I checked when I ran into this problem 2 months ago.  Unfortunately, I don't think I want to replace the exhaust headers quite yet.<P>fieroX, I will keep an eye on your site.  Keep me posted.  I have been trying to find a way to fabricate a system that will work with the limited room.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I simply brought up what we had to offer so that you do not have to re-invent the wheel, it will bolt in directly to what you have now<P>------------------<BR>Technician, West Coast Fiero<BR>www.cwestco.com<BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000007||Banzai||12-11-2001||06:39 AM||||95 and up camaro's and I think later c4 vettes used a small cat(they had two) on the left bank hooked directly to the exaust manifold. I don't know if it's enough by itself to clean up the 3800.<BR>Good Luck<P>Banzai !!!!!!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000008||skitime||12-11-2001||08:09 AM||||Wahooo!!!!!!! I just got my West Coast Fiero 3800 headers yesterday and they are sweeeet. Thanks so much West Coast Fiero. I wanted a complete exhaust system with a cat and a real muffler installed like a stock system. Nearly every 3800 swap I have seen are either skipping the cat and  going right into a small muffler because the 3800 manifold dumps on the trunk side or they just go through a cat or two and through resonator tips.  These headers drop in the stock Fiero headpipe location and are ready for a 2 1/2 exhaust system.  I can't wait to hear them purrrr and feel the power increase.  If you want the best exhaust system go with these.<P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature-2.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by skitime (edited 12-11-2001).]||||reg||1
