Z||000010||TTiger||12-11-2001||03:11 PM||||HMMM, now you all got me thinking.  Anyone know if the exhaust manifolds on a 92 Bonneville 3800SC are interchangable?  Might be a long shot, but I have somewhat of an idea.  <P>West Coast Fiero, I will definately keep that system in mind.  I may have to go that route after Christmas, when I have the funds.  That exhaust does look sweet  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_drool.gif"><P>Tony||||reg||3
Z||000011||West Coast Fiero||12-16-2001||01:03 AM||||the usuall time in the past from placing the order to arriving on your doorstep was no less than 1 week, but no later than 2. However we have streamlined the fabrication process here as the header flanges are now made in house utilizing a Bridgeport automated C&C. So as a rough estimate ( including our newly aquired FedEx online service ) would be a possiblity of 1 week. On a side note, we have just recently contracted out HyTech coating wich will provide a mirror finish ceramic coating on all exhaust header systems for an additional $200.<P><P>------------------<BR>Technician, West Coast Fiero<BR>www.cwestco.com<BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
