Z||000020||West Coast Fiero||12-16-2001||08:48 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by terryk:<BR><B>West Coast Fiero:<P>What's the Carb EO number for the headers? These would make life easier.<P>TK</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I do not have that information at this time, but as we all know sir, the 3800 series engines were not original equipment in the Pontiac Fiero, therefore no 3800 equipment would be EO? or CARB certified for the vehicle unless made as a direct replacement item for the donor vehicle i.e. Bonneville, Regal, Grand Prix, etc. One of the qualifing circumstances is that the items in question must have smog and EGR adaptations, which our 3800 headers do.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://clubs.hemmings.com/fieroswest/WestCoast300.gif">  <BR>Eric Nelson<BR>Technician,<BR>West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111<p>[This message has been edited by West Coast Fiero (edited 12-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000021||Orville||12-18-2001||01:49 PM||||Eric, to follow up on Terryk's Question, have <BR>you recently gotten the carb ref's to pass a<BR>3800 swap that has these non stock exhaust<BR>manifolds?||||reg||7
Z||000022||Orville||12-18-2001||01:58 PM||||Eric, to follow up on Teryk's question, have<BR>you recently gotten the carb ref's to pass a<BR>3800 swap with non stock exaust manifolds?||||reg||7
Z||000023||terryk||12-18-2001||03:21 PM||||Sir? Is my dad on the forum now?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>You said the headers are "smog legal." I would assume you mean "except in California" if there is no EO.<P>I was just hoping you have an EO so the headers would be legal in California. I don't think headers are considered non-emissions related according to BAR.<P>Let us know. This will be great! I'm tired of having to remove the non-EO stuff or hoping they don't notice during testing. Up here (Sac) they are getting pretty tight.<P>According to my BAR contact, EO aftermarket parts are legal on recertified engine swaps. Are you getting different information? <P>TK<BR><p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 12-18-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000024||West Coast Fiero||12-18-2001||08:56 PM||||I personnaly do not have the details on the exhaust system as these are Steve Childer's creation here at WCF. Chris West has all the info to answer any questions you may have.<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://clubs.hemmings.com/fieroswest/WestCoast300.gif"> <BR>Eric Nelson<BR>Technician,<BR>West Coast Fiero<BR>www.cwestco.com<BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
